value.description:
Identifier matching the type: CVE ID / 40-char hex / ecosystem:name@version. Comma-separated for a batch; duplicates are removed automatically.
Ecosystems must use the exact, case-sensitive registry name: npm, PyPI, Maven, NuGet, RubyGems, crates.io, Go, Packagist, Hex, Pub, CRAN. Maven uses Maven:groupId:artifactId@version; OS packages usually need a release suffix such as Debian:12 or Alpine:v3.16.
To make sure every item is checked, pass at most 5 CVE IDs or 1000 package entries per call.
An empty list can also mean a misspelled name or version, so verify the spelling before concluding there is no vulnerability.
e.g.
{"type": "cve", "value": "CVE-2021-44228"}
{"type": "package", "value": "PyPI:jinja2@2.4.1"}
{"type": "commit", "value": "6879efc2c1596d11a6a6ad296f80063b558d5e0f"}
